From 35533ef2cca9510a9f34cd5492f83801fc0408f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andelib Taref Ababa <88821308+IamAndelib@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:31:24 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Don't abort the input method on damaged or unwritable
 user data

Several unwrap()s on user data panic, and a panic across the C FFI aborts
the host input method process. Each of these failures happened on every
activation until the user deleted the file by hand:

- a truncated or invalid phonetic-candidate-selection.json
- a truncated or invalid user autocorrect.json, at load and at every word
  start
- a selection file that can't be written (read-only dir, full disk, path
  is a directory)
- an unparsable fixed layout file (e.g. a half-written user import)

Treat unreadable selection/autocorrect files as empty and stop retrying
until the file changes. Save selections through a temporary file and a
rename so a crash can't leave a truncated file. Never store a selection
with an empty key or value (committing the literal ":)" stored {":": ""}).
Drop such entries, and values doubled by the old suffix bug, when loading.
Fall back to Avro Phonetic when a fixed layout can't be parsed.

FixedMethod::new() now returns Option. The unused, panicking
utility::read() is removed.
